Historical MySQL installation sources
====================================

This directory retains upstream schemas, versioned migrations and prefix
datasets for MySQL 5.x. install-db.sh records the old 1.4.0 -> 1.9.5 chain.
These historical files do not reconstruct the current release and must not
be imported into an A2Billing 3.0 (nixonch) database.

The canonical A2Billing 3.0 (nixonch) schema and initial data are maintained directly in
../mysql-8.x/a2billing-install.sql. Installation instructions are in
../mysql-8.x/INFO.

Maintainer-only export and validation
------------------------------------

build-install.py normalizes or validates the canonical SQL using a separate
test MySQL 8.0 server. End users do not need this tool, Python or the historical
files. Do not use the production server.

From mysql-5.x/, run:

    python3 build-install.py --socket=/path/to/test/mysql.sock
    python3 build-install.py --socket=/path/to/test/mysql.sock --check

Add --mysql=/path/to/mysql and --mysqldump=/path/to/mysqldump if clients are
outside PATH. --user overrides the default root account. MYSQL_PWD can supply
a password if required.

By default, the tool imports the canonical SQL into a uniquely named temporary
a2b_install_build_* database, exports final definitions and seed data, and
drops only that database. --check compares the normalized SQL without writing.
Use the same MySQL 8.0 version for byte-for-byte checks.

--from-database=a2b_NAME can export an existing test database with version 3.0 (nixonch);
that database is read without modification and is not dropped. It must contain
only installation schema and seed data, never production or test activity.
